      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s core characterization of politeness as “the use of socially expected courteous language” is not explicitly supported in the packet text.",
        "The packet mentions “politeness markers that are mandatory in human communities” and “defensive impression management strategies (such as hedges),” but it does not define politeness as a “help-seeking strategy,” nor does it explicitly link politeness to “managing impressions during requests or questions.”",
        "The packet discusses changes in help-seeking strategies in AI vs. human settings, but the definition presents a general functional description (“functions as a help-seeking strategy…”) that is broader than what the packet directly states."
